[19.3914, "o", "er minute per IP.\u001b[8;68H                                                    \u001b[9;68H                                                    \u001b[10;68H\u001b[38;5;3;49m\u203a Checkout is getting hammered by bots. Add per-IP\u001b[39;49m  \u001b[11;68H\u001b[38;5;3;49mrate limiting to POST /checkout.\u001b[39;49m                    \u001b[12;68H                                                    \u001b[13;68HI'll add a token-bucket limiter backed by the       \u001b[14;68Hexisting Redis cache, 10 requests per minute per IP.\u001b[15;68H                                                    \u001b[16;68H\u001b[38;5;3;49m\u203a Sounds good, keep the limit configurable.\u001b[39;49m         \u001b[17;68H                                                    \u001b[18;68HAdded RATE_LIMIT_PER_MIN to config and wired the    \u001b[19;68Hmiddleware. Before I run the load test against      \u001b[20;68Hstaging, can I hit https://staging.example.test?    \u001b[21;68H                                                    \u001b[22;68H                                                    \u001b[23;68H                                     "]
